 "title": "Don't Punish the Behavior You Want to See",
 "topic": "mindset",
 "summary": "This video is a skit illustrating how people often unintentionally push away the very behavior they want by making others feel bad when they show up. The creator claims that instead of punishing people, you should reward the behavior you want so they are more likely to repeat it.",
 "key_points": [
  "Don't punish the behavior you want to see.",
  "If you want someone to spend more time with you, don't make him feel bad when he actually does.",
  "Making someone feel bad when they show up trains them to want to spend less time with you.",
  "If you reward the behavior you want, people are more likely to want to repeat that behavior.",
  "Example of rewarding desired behavior: telling someone \"We're so glad to see you bro, we missed you!\" when they show up."
 ],
 "content": "Post text: Don’t punish the behavior you want to see! 😮 Transcript: Speaker 1: Hey, what's up guys? Speaker 2: Oh, look who finally decided to spend time with us! Speaker 1: Oh, don't mind him, dude. We're glad you're here. We really missed you, bro. [20 Minutes Later] Speaker 1: Yo, I'm gonna go to the bathroom quick. I'll be back. Speaker 3: All right, man. Speaker 2: Yo, bro, why'd you tell him \"Don't mind him\" earlier? Speaker 3: I meant what I said! I'm just mad because he's not really spending as much time with us ever since his new business idea. Speaker 2: Then don't punish the behavior you want to see. Speaker 3: What do you mean? Speaker 2: Look, I'm just saying, man, if you want him to spend more time with us, don't make him feel bad when he actually does. That just trains him to want to spend less time with us. I've learned that with people, if you reward the behavior you want, they're more likely to want to repeat that behavior. That's why when he showed up I was like, \"We're so glad to see you, bro, we missed you!\" Speaker 3: I like that, man. You just earned another follower! Text on screen: Hey what's up guys?, Oh! Look who finally decided to spend time with us!, Don't mind him dude. We're glad you're here. We really missed you bro., 20 Minutes Later, Yo I'm gonna go to the bathroom quick. I'll be back, Yo bro why'd you tell him \"Don't mind him\" earlier?, I meant what I said! I'm just mad because he's not really spending as much time with us, Ever since his new business idea., Then don't punish the behavior you want to see., What do you mean?, Look I'm just saying man, if you want him to spend more time with us, don't make him feel bad when he actually does., That just trains him to want to spend less time with us.. I've learned that with people if you reward the behavior you want.., They're more likely to want to repeat that behavior. That's why when he showed up I said, \"We're so glad to see you bro we missed you!\", I like that man. You just earned another follower!",
